---
// Readability vs Optimization balance + Asymptotic Big-O crossover vs real hardware constants.
const W = 900;
const H = 278;
---
<figure class="ge8b">
  <div class="ge8b-scroll">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Comparing efficiency versus readability trade-offs and when Big-O asymptotic complexity beats O(N) linear CPU cache scans.">
      {/* Left panel: Big-O vs Small-N cache constants */}
      <rect x="14" y="14" width="428" height="250" rx="10" class="ge8b-card" />
      <text x="30" y="42" class="ge8b-h">
        <tspan data-lang-en>1. Big-O Crossover vs. Real Hardware Constants</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>1. Đừng tin mù Big-O: Ngưỡng giao cắt với phần cứng</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="60" width="396" height="62" rx="6" class="ge8b-box is-ok" />
      <text x="44" y="80" class="ge8b-b-ok">Small N (&lt;= 16..32 keys): O(N) slice scan wins!</text>
      <text x="44" y="99" class="ge8b-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Contiguous slice fits inside L1 cache lines (~1 ns/step).</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Duyệt thẳng slice nằm gọn L1 cache, nhanh hơn băm map!</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="132" width="396" height="62" rx="6" class="ge8b-box" />
      <text x="44" y="152" class="ge8b-b">Large N (&gt;= 1,000 keys): O(1) map / O(log N) wins!</text>
      <text x="44" y="171" class="ge8b-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>As N grows, algorithmic complexity dominates fixed constant factors.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Khi dữ liệu phình lớn, độ phức tạp O(log N) bứt tốc bỏ xa O(N).</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="204" width="396" height="46" rx="6" class="ge8b-box" />
      <text x="44" y="224" class="ge8b-b">Rule: Know data sizes inside your RAER spec before choosing.</text>

      {/* Right panel: Readability vs Efficiency */}
      <rect x="460" y="14" width="426" height="250" rx="10" class="ge8b-card" />
      <text x="476" y="42" class="ge8b-h">
        <tspan data-lang-en>2. Protecting Readability &amp; Maintainability</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>2. Giữ code sạch đẹp sau khi tối ưu xong</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="476" y="60" width="394" height="58" rx="6" class="ge8b-box is-ok" />
      <text x="490" y="80" class="ge8b-b-ok">Encapsulate fast-path complexity behind tiny APIs</text>
      <text x="490" y="99" class="ge8b-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Hide buffer reuse / byte scans behind clean helper names.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Giấu phần đọc buffer khéo léo sau tên hàm rõ như Sum6Reader.</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="476" y="128" width="394" height="58" rx="6" class="ge8b-box" />
      <text x="490" y="148" class="ge8b-b">Attach benchmark + WHY comment on tricky invariants</text>
      <text x="490" y="167" class="ge8b-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Cite RAER gains so future PRs never revert critical code.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Ghi rõ số đo PR để người sau không "refactor" làm chậm lại.</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="476" y="196" width="394" height="54" rx="6" class="ge8b-box is-red" />
      <text x="490" y="216" class="ge8b-b-red">If speed gain &lt; RAER pain yet bug risk spikes → Roll back!</text>
      <text x="490" y="234" class="ge8b-m">Keep boring, readable Go code everywhere outside hot paths.</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Asymptotic Big-O predicts growth trends while CPU cache constants pick winners at small sizes; encapsulate fast paths with documented benchmarks so maintainable code stays easy to audit.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Độ phức tạp Big-O quyết định tốc độ ở dữ liệu lớn, còn phần cứng CPU quyết định ở kích thước nhỏ; luôn gói phần code tối ưu sau interface sạch kèm comment số đo thay vì viết rối cả dự án.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .ge8b { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .ge8b-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .ge8b svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .ge8b text { font-size: 12px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .ge8b-card { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .ge8b-box { fill: var(--bg); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .ge8b-box.is-red { stroke: var(--red); fill: var(--red-tint-bg); }
  .ge8b-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .ge8b-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .ge8b-h { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .ge8b-b { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .ge8b-b-red { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--red); }
  .ge8b-b-ok { font-weight: 700; fill: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .ge8b-b-ok { fill: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .ge8b-m { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 11px; }
  .ge8b figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
